# React Flow viewer (browser demo)

Canonical decisions: sibling monorepo
`executioncontrolprotocol/packages/extensions/format-reactflow/REACTFLOW_RENDER.md`
(or local copy under that package path).

## Must follow

- Render `ecp-step` and projected `ecp-io` nodes (Inputs always; Outputs when `returns` is set, plus a demo empty Outputs node so the first parameter can be added). Ignore group wrappers.
- Draw only data edges with both `sourceHandle` and `targetHandle`.
- Every schema port gets a handle: hollow if unconnected, solid if connected. Outputs handles are target-only.
- Idle routes: solid cyan matching input handles (`--color-tertiary-fixed-dim`).
- During run: marching ants on in-flight edges; green when source step completed.
- Node pulse: soft, low-spread shadow on **running** only; keep a clear green completed glow.
- Do not open the state modal on Run click — open when the run finishes (or when `accepts` needs a form); keep **Inspect state** in the zoom/fit Controls.
- Configure dialog (steps): removable literals after save, add unbound Zod params, editable `as` with ref rewrite; save via `ecp.patch` + `syncFromManifest`.
- Configure dialog (I/O): patch `workflow.accepts` / `workflow.returns`, not `steps[id]`. Add/remove/rename schema properties. Renaming an accepts key rewrites `state.<old>` refs.
- Canvas connect: output→input writes `$ref` into target `step.input` (Fluent `ref(...)`); Inputs source uses the property name (`ref("prompt")`). Dropping onto an occupied handle **replaces** the previous connection. Click a route to select it; the mid-path ellipsis (or right-click) opens **Delete connection**. Backspace/Delete also removes that binding — never delete step nodes from the canvas. Connect to Outputs patches `returns` so the property name matches source `.as()`. Same patch + sync path. Do not treat RF edges as source of truth—re-encode after patch.
- Outputs ports with a source show `← {refPath}` like step inputs. Skip that label on the `+` placeholder.
- Connect type compatibility (demo-local): match `portTypeKind` from `valueSchema`/`typeLabel` (`number`≡`integer`; `unknown` pairs with anything). During output drag, grey + cross incompatible inputs (`ecp-rf-port--incompatible` / `ecp-rf-handle--incompatible`); `isValidConnection` + `isConnectable` reject them. Do not reject a second connection just because the target handle is already connected.
- Run form widgets from `accepts` (same `valueSchema` mapping as configure). Inspect shows `result.output` when `returns` is set.
- Map editors from port **`valueSchema`** (demo-local); fall back to `typeLabel`. Never put widget names in the encode document.
  - short `string` → text input; long (`prompt`/`system`/… or length/`\n`) → textarea
  - `object`/`array`/unknown → Monaco JSON; `number` → number input; `boolean` → toggle
  - `string`+`enum` ≤4 → radios; >4 → `<select>`; `array`+`items.enum` → checkbox multi-select
